# Temporal pipeline state (runtime evidence — must survive deploys).
#
# Why this pattern matters for deploy survival: hadoku_site's
# deploy-executor runs `git stash --include-untracked` before pulling
# main, and never pops the stash. UNTRACKED files get stashed away.
# IGNORED files (matching these patterns) are skipped by stash and
# survive on disk across deploys.
#
# 2026-04-28: an entire batch of phase5-prod-v* state was wiped during
# a deploy because the prior pattern list (smoke-*, batch-*,
# crimson-kitty-*, phase4-external-v*) was too narrow. Generalized to
# `state/*/` so any future batch-naming convention is protected by
# default. Files at the root of state/ remain visible unless explicitly
# tracked; existing tracked files under any state subdir keep tracking.
state/*/

# Temporary
.tmp/
.cache/

# per-repo vault key (Phase 2 of per-key ACL plan; never commit)
.devvault.local.json
.playwright-mcp/
